{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/345652-mecha-suit-endowments-can-they-work","id":345652,"title":"Mecha Suit Endowments: can they work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T03:44:53-08:00","id":345652,"title":"Mecha Suit Endowments: can they work?","content":"I am talking about human sized Mechas, by the way. I saw this question on the WhiteWolf subreddit (<a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/2prbpa/are_there_any_probably_homebrew_mecha_expansions/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG...ha_expansions/</a>) and I thought that it was a neat idea, though maybe a bit too flashy for the WoD. Do you think that such Mechas would be more or less standardized, with cosmetic changes based on the Conspiracy, or actually give different mechanical benefits for each Conspiracy? Any ideas for crunch are also welcome. I'll see if I can think of some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:06:48-08:00","id":345720,"title":"","content":"I would consider enviromentally sealed Powered Armor to be less flashy and a good addition to Advanced Armory (you could limit the number of suits to less than 10 though). The Vigil's system of R&amp;D I think could be good enough to model them given there are provisions for Armor Endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T18:18:05-08:00","id":346278,"title":"","content":"Mecha would realistically be way too powerful for endowments. <br /> <br /> A tank has what, 30 or so points of armor according to armory? If you can make 30 points worth of armor cost 10 merit points or less using the endowment system you must be using some really impressive math, and then of course a mecha ought to have weapons capable of taking out their competition, and may or may not be able to fly.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that giving hunters mecha is wrong hurting fun, but I would no more make having a mecha be an endowment than I would someone having their own tank or fighter jet as an endowment.<br /> <br /> My personal suggestion, because I have also thought about a mechanized nwod game, would be to use the spaceship rules from Infinite Macabre: It would be a merit, with four subtraits- size, armor, speed, and weaponry. <br /> <br /> Unless someone is just being a valkyrie fanboy, then if valkyrie has mecha then cainites can summon blood mecha, lucifuge can summon demon mecha, vanguard can make psychic exoskeletons, the inquisition can summon angel mecha, cheiron has biomecha, etc. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:09:25-08:00","id":346466,"title":"","content":"To borrow terms from Shadowrun: Sometimes, you just gotta let that pink mohawk fly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:16:29-08:00","id":346468,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to have -30- armor. GottaGo's talking about a power armor <b>suit</b>, it doesn't have to be appreciably better than what's already out there, just environmentally sealed, with a camera system so that supernatural creatures can't make eye contact, and maybe something a little extra for some oomph. Have you seen these things? They run as fast as a car, can take shotgun blasts to the head, and some of them can turn invisible, teleport, or merge with a car and empty out your chest with a drill, and that's just the weaker things. Take some of that exo-stuff they're working up in Japan, slap some armor plates on that thing. Download the plans for one of those microwave guns off the internet. Do everything you're not <i>supposed</i> to do because it's against the Geneva convention and pull it out of your pants because not a thing out there is paying attention. We're not talking about valkyries here, we're talking about some body armor that helps hold you up and maybe looks like hell when you're using it. Just because that seven-foot-tall meat <i>thing</i> that turned Frank's insides into a meaty salad before it jumped up onto the roof, grew wings made of squealing, living cockroaches, and buzzed off into the night.<br /> <br /> Endowment: The Suit<br /> It's the last suit you'll ever wear. Created through combined technologies of multiple corporate conglomerates and now left to you, the suit is tailored for your body and comes in any number of fun, festive colors. It seals up everything about you - thumbprints, voice pattern, breath rate, heat map, eye contact, it's all gone when you wear The Suit. You put this baby on at its base and it's as good as any of those monsters out there once you charge it up. Just don't power down when you're in the wrong place.<br /> Armor: For each dot of Armor, The Suit gets 1 more rank in armor. You can apply this to its ballistic or impact armor. The Suit starts with a value of 3/2<br /> Speed: For each dot of Speed, The Suit gets +2 speed over your normal speed.<br /> Weaponry: For each dot of Weaponry, the suit can be loaded with a new weapon. This can be any weapon you can buy yourself and mounted to The Suit.<br /> Special Weaponry: Treat this like the Token Merit for what weapons it can buy.<br /> <br /> Modules<br /> These components add new features to the suit, such as flight, experimental weapons, aa unique appearance, and other such things. You have to buy them in the cash shop.<br /> <br /> Holy shit, Hunter conspiracy based off those live-action social network games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T21:40:37-08:00","id":347158,"title":"","content":"There are cars that have speed ratings of 301 in nwod, plus 2 ain't going to cover that any time soon. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T21:19:49-08:00","id":347983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/345652-mecha-suit-endowments-can-they-work?p=347158#post347158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are cars that have speed ratings of 301 in nwod, plus 2 ain't going to cover that any time soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know very well that the likelihood of a suit of power armor (and a player power) needing to top 200 MPH is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:11:50-08:00","id":348338,"title":"","content":"Generally I take Armor chart in GMC, see how Flak Armor is represented there, compare it with Warhammer 40K RPG's Flak Armor, compare the latter's Flak Armor with Powered Armor designed for humans, and scale things appropriately for GMC. By that logic Powered Armor in GMC could have even twice the Armor rating of Flak Armor of GMC, but this needs further analysis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:22:43-08:00","id":348697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/345652-mecha-suit-endowments-can-they-work?p=347983#post347983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know very well that the likelihood of a suit of power armor (and a player power) needing to top 200 MPH is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, what I know is ridiculous is calling something as fast as a car in the fluff and then providing rules that makes them inferior to that.<br /> <br /> The suit also really needs a structure rating. With other valkyrie equipment it's not that much of an oversight, their ray gun gets broken they pull out another weapon, but when a suit of power armor gets broken the guy in it is a fish in a barrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:56:26-08:00","id":348730,"title":"","content":"I think there's a body armor prototype write-up up in Armory Reloaded (p.143, &quot;Gladiator&quot;) that can work as a base for a mech-suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T10:43:47-08:00","id":349162,"title":"","content":"When designing a suit the fact it might strain the body could be also taken into the account. You could have more powerful prototype design, but with adverse effects on human body. Price to pay for keeping up with all those more physically able supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T20:26:59-08:00","id":352277,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Advanced Armory: Berserkr Skin (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <br /> In the backlogs of Taskforce: VALKYRIES armory are a few failed projects; whether they were too expensive, too temperamental, or too dangerous varies from piece to piece, but the point stands - not everything made for the Vigil is exactly stable.<br /> <br /> The Berserkr Skin Personal Armor System is a prime example; standing an imposing 8 feet tall and weighing three-quarters of a ton, it was intended to allow a Hunter to stand toe-to-toe with the monsters. In some respects, they succeeded; the armor is fully hermetically sealed and sports 360-degree vision, thanks to a suite of cameras run by a small battery. It supplies 1/1 armor and a tank of air that'll last for days. Of course, the sheer weight means that the wearer lowers their Defense and Speed by 3 each, and that they cannot Dodge or run; the composite view generated from the cameras also tends to disorient and the fingers are a bit clumsy, inflicting a -2 penalty to all Perception rolls and actions requiring fine manipulation while it is worn.<br /> <br /> However, a Hunter with a RFID chip that's wearing the armor can power it up for a scene; a light electrical current courses through the skin of the suit, hardening it into plates, while servos engage and the hunter gets a sharp stab in the back of their neck as fiber-optic cables embed themselves in their nerves. While so engaged, the normal drawbacks of wearing the suit disappear as sensory information is piped into their brains and pneumatic musculature makes the armor as responsive as a second skin.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it supplies a definite boost to the Hunter - the Armor rating improves to 3/3, and they enjoy a +2 bonus to Strength and Speed; the neural connection also stokes endorphin production, allowing them to enjoy the benefits (and drawbacks) of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=223525#post223525\">Drugged - Stimulant</a> Tilt while it is engaged.<br /> <br /> There are several reasons why the Skin wasn't put into general use; first of all, it is hellishly expensive to make. Economics aside, it also is harmful to the wearer. Switching the Berserkr Skin on costs one Willpower and inflicts 1L damage as it integrates itself into the wearer's autonomic systems. Worse, they lose another point of Willpower and take another level of Lethal damage at the end of the scene when it switches off; thanks to torn muscles and blood loss, the user then suffers the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=148270#post148270\">Fatigue</a> condition as well. Theoretically, re-engaging the suit can negate the Fatigue; however, the suit only holds enough juice for about an hour of operation - and that includes the power-down cycle.There are stories swapped around about agents who had to be cut out of their suit after re-engaging it.<br /> <br /> There's also the small matter of sterility, miscarriages, and an increased chance of cancer; there wasn't enough room for proper radiation shielding for the power cells, which emit just enough radiation to cause problems. <hr /><br /> Theoretically, these problems could be sorted out during your chronicle; perhaps some captured mad science could supply some answers. In that case, the upgrades would cost another 3 Merit dots. However, an upgraded suit would last all night, would give a +3 bonus to Speed rather than a +2, would inflict Bashing damage instead of Lethal, and would give <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=145773#post145773\">Winded</a> instead of Fatigue once operation was completed.<br /> <br /> More pertinently to most Cells, a success on a Dexterity + Crafts roll can attach equipment to the suit - and 10 Successes on an extended Intelligence + Computers roll wires the controls for that equipment into the suit's &quot;nervous system.&quot; There are, apparently, very few sensations <i>quite</i> like firing a missile with your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-29-2014, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T05:44:47-08:00","id":352574,"title":"","content":"Now you just need to put a big chaingun and a missile launcher on it. You can never know. Plus, it's a genre convention. Especially the missiles, for some reason (TFV ever had a bad encounter with a Great Old One?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4626-xenoheart","name":"Xenoheart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:46:08-08:00","id":352620,"title":"","content":"Cheiron does not field class powered armor suits, but either ones made from skinned supernaturals (think of Arata quinque in Tokyo Ghoul) or uses nanomachines instead of supernatural implants for variety. They respond to physical trauma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:40:31-08:00","id":353003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenoheart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/345652-mecha-suit-endowments-can-they-work?p=352574#post352574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you just need to put a big chaingun and a missile launcher on it. You can never know. Plus, it's a genre convention. Especially the missiles, for some reason (TFV ever had a bad encounter with a Great Old One?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll toss in a note about jury-rigging something together - just wire a weapon in, bypassing the normal triggering mechanism. It's more of a semi-armored space suit than a full-on mech.<br /> <hr /><br /> As for Cheiron... Fallen Dragon + NGE. 'nuff said.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Fine, fine, I'll whip something up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T13:30:14-08:00","id":353055,"title":"","content":"Hey, sometimes it's just critical to be armed to take down a hard, blindingly fast, high-flying biomechanical monstrosity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4626-xenoheart","name":"Xenoheart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T15:48:23-08:00","id":353207,"title":"","content":"Looking at it again, I think that Cheiron wouldn't have mechs - it isn't inside their schtick, as it were. They're all about grafting parts onto their operatives, not general, free-standing biotech. While biomechs are cool, they aren't what Cheiron <i>does</i>...<br /> <br /> Really, the only canon conspiracies that &quot;click&quot; with having Mecha are AKD and TFV, since both of them have an aesthetic involving external artifacts. Of the other conspiracies...<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones, Cheiron Group, Les Mysteres, and Lucifuge all have &quot;Mecha&quot; Endowments in the form of powerful personal buffs that fill the same roll.<br /> <br /> The others... are more spellcast-y than the above, or are just really, really specific (Cainite Heresy and Knights of St. George, I'm looking at you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T08:25:29-08:00","id":353761,"title":"","content":"You know, I forgot to eyeball the Berserkr Skin - the upgrade is <i>definitely</i> not worth 5 dots. I'll go fix that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T02:36:01-08:00","id":357356,"title":"","content":"You know what? I can't leave well enough alone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Thaumotechnology - Corpse Suits (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group has barely scratched <i>the surface</i> of what Artificial Organics are capable of. However, they <i>have</i> figured out that if you stick them on an artificial bone frame, and hook up a small current and a little bit of vitriol... Well, the results are simply <i>astounding</i>.<br /> <br /> A Corpse Suit appears to be the skin of a human being, cured and stitched together in differing patches; a Hunter with a Vitriol Pump can climb inside one and plug it into the pump, bringing its circulatory system online. It might not be the <i>prettiest</i> piece of equipment, but it gets the job done.<br /> <br /> By putting the suit on and &quot;plugging it in&quot;, the Hunter wearing it gains the benefits of the Absorb Energy (Electricity), Dead Flesh, and Titan's Strength Dread Powers at 4 dots each; their Brawl attacks also deal Lethal damage, gaining a +1 weapon bonus. However, each scene of continuous use consumes a use of the Hunter's Vitriol Pump and requires that a small 9-volt battery is embedded in the slot near the back.<br /> <br /> What Cheiron does <i>not</i> put in their literature is the dreams - violent dreams, of being dug up and cut up and stitched together. Each time a Hunter uses a Corpse Suit, they risk Disquiet; the suit does not roll its (non-existent) Potency, instead gaining a single Success. The Disquiet generated by wearing the suit is targeted against the Hunter themselves*; Hate and Fear are common forms of Disquiet, but others have been recorded (and quietly hushed up by R&amp;D, who <i>swear</i> they've almost ironed that little wrinkle out...) <hr /><br /> * Since it is, for all practical intents and purposes, impossible to not interact with yourself for a week, the Disquiet Condition can also be resolved by not wearing the suit for a week. Valuable employees (and/or those with the <i>special</i> medical package) are allotted mandatory psychological screening and vacation time for a <i>reason</i>, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 01-13-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:28:31-08:00","id":368692,"title":"","content":"This whole thread reminds me of Xcom:EW's MEc Troopers.<br /> <br /> and with some WoD paint and some balancing tweaks i think they could fit.<br /> <br /> or reference: The Trooper: <a href=\"http://xcom.wikia.com/wiki/MEC_Trooper\" target=\"_blank\">http://xcom.wikia.com/wiki/MEC_Trooper</a><br /> <br /> their Suit: <a href=\"http://xcom.wikia.com/wiki/MEC\" target=\"_blank\">http://xcom.wikia.com/wiki/MEC</a><br /> <br /> <br /> yeah they are REALLY strong... but they arent subtle, and this IS the WoD we are talking about, they are just a step above humans in the power scale IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4218-hammbone87","name":"Hammbone87","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}